    Traditional Chinese Spring Onion Pancakes

    Makes 2 Large Pancakes

    Use Vegetable Oil instead of Lard to make them Vegetarian

    Try different fillings such as Laoganma or nuts

Ingredients:

    Dough:
        150g Plain Flour
        105g Luke Warm Water
        2g Salt

    Roux:
        16g Plain Flour
        60g Lard

    Filling:
        2 Spring Onions Finely Chopped

Method:

    Melt the lard and add the plain flour to make the roux and then leave to cool

    Add the dough ingredients to a stand mixer and mix until smooth

    Rest the dough for 30 mins

    Divide the dough in half and roll each out to a long thing rectangle

    Spread the roux in the centre leaving approx. 1cm around the edges

    Sprinkle the spring onion over the rough

    Roll the dough up like a long siss roll and coil to form a disc

    Lightly roll out the disc to form the pancake

    Pan fry in more lard until crispy and brown on both sides

